            <div xml:id="d293">

                <pb facs="0372" n="268" sameAs="frus:frus1932v03/pg268"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/4085: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan (Forbes) to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-02-10T17:00:00+09:00">February 10, 1932—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received February 10—6:20 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>58. The Military Attaché has been informed by the General Staff office that it
                    has been decided that the 9th Division which has been under preparation for
                    departure is to leave for Shanghai. He was further informed that in view of
                    movements of the Chinese fugitive soldiers in the vicinity of Harbin it has been
                    decided that the 2d Division <pb facs="0373" n="269" xml:id="pg269"/> remain
                    there for the time being until peace and order are restored, the other troops to
                    return to their original stations as soon as possible.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Forbes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
